course: dictionary
lesson: 15446
title: Stone that tells a story
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A stele (say it steel-ee) is a tall stone slab or pillar with writing or carvings on it. People long ago stood steles up so everyone could read them.
explain: «The king had a stele carved with the names of his great victories.» Built to tell everyone and carved with names are clues: a stele is a message in stone.
explain: Stele is also a word in plant science. There it means the central core of a root or stem, which carries water and food. «Water travels up the stele inside the root.» The subject tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Stele is a noun. Its plural can be stelae or steles.
fact: In history, a stele is an upright stone slab or pillar with writing or carvings, often put up as a monument, gravestone or record.
fact: Hammurabi's law code is carved on a stele, so people could read the laws.
fact: The Rosetta Stone is part of a stele.
fact: In botany, the stele is the central core of a plant's root or stem, which carries water and food.
exercise: «The ancient king had a stele carved with the laws of the land.» What is a stele? | *An upright stone slab with writing or carvings on it | A kind of woolly blanket | A bird that lives in the desert | A soft wooden boat
exercise: In a plant lesson, the teacher says, «Water moves up through the stele.» What does stele mean here? | A stone pillar with writing carved on it | *The central core of a plant's root or stem, which carries water | A type of flower petal | A small green leaf
exercise: Which is a correct plural of stele? | stile | *stelae | stellar | steal
test: «The Maya carved the names of their rulers on a tall stele.» What was the stele used for? | To bake bread for the village | To hold up a roof | *To record the names of their rulers | To keep the rain off their boats
test: In botany, what does the stele of a root carry? | Sand and stones | Air and smoke | *Water and food | Sound and heat
exam: «Hammurabi's laws were carved on a stele so everyone could read them.» Which meaning fits stele best? | A river that runs through the desert | A soft cloth used to wrap a baby | A type of sandwich | *A tall stone slab with writing carved on it
